  "warnings": [
    "lineage agent notes: 1) Version pick (lines 101-104): ROW_NUMBER orders by updated_at, _row_seq ascending and keeps version_no = 1. That keeps the OLDEST version saved up to @AsOfDate, not the current one the comments promise (CR-1702). The PySpark port must copy the ascending order to match the legacy output. 2) initials (line 124): SUBSTRING(x, 0, 2) returns only the first character. T-SQL counts positions 0 and 1 and keeps the 1 character that exists, so in Spark use substring(x,1,1). 3) email_shared_count is counted over the surviving rows in #customer (one per customer), not over all versions. Matching is case- and collation-sensitive according to the database collation. 4) version_count counts only the versions with CAST(updated_at AS DATE) <= @AsOfDate. 5) age_at_join uses DATEDIFF(YEAR), which counts year boundaries crossed, not completed years. 6) segment_code is CHAR(4), and T-SQL ignores trailing spaces in comparisons, so 'STD ' = 'STD' is true. Spark needs rtrim. In the same way, LEN() ignores trailing spaces in the eircode check. 7) first_name is RTRIMmed but last_name is not (line 122). 8) The read uses NOLOCK, so it can pick up rows that are not yet committed. customer_id is listed as a ranks edge because it is the ROW_NUMBER partition key."
